---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/paths';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="What The Huntspeak Project is, who it’s for, and how to take part."
  current="about"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1 class="page-title">About The Huntspeak Project</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">
      We are a community building learnable Huntspeak from a handful of official lines in Final Fantasy XIV —
      scraps turned into something you can use in roleplay and storytelling.
    </p>

    <p>
      The game tells us Huntspeak ranges from hunt signals (clicks and whistles) to a full spoken tongue,
      that it differs between Seekers of the Sun and Keepers of the Moon, and that only a few tribes
      still use the full language. Most of what you’ll find here expands that foundation from a
      Moon / Keeper leaning — without pretending to be Square Enix canon.
    </p>

    <p>
      We sometimes call the hunt-signal side <span class="hs">Khiädyasa</span> (“hunt-voice”) and the
      full spoken language <span class="hs">Shilyasa</span> (“near-voice”). Those names are still
      settling; the lessons on this site teach the full spoken language.
    </p>

    <h2>Community</h2>
    <p>
      Come talk Huntspeak, share roleplay lines, and help grow the language with us on
      <a href="https://discord.gg/bG9dGBHFtS" rel="noopener noreferrer">Discord</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Where to go next</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={withBase('/learn/')}>Start learning</a></li>
      <li><a href={withBase('/phrasebook/')}>Phrasebook</a></li>
      <li><a href={withBase('/dictionary/')}>Dictionary</a></li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://discord.gg/bG9dGBHFtS" rel="noopener noreferrer">Discord</a>
        — the living community
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/L1ghth0us3/The-Huntspeak-Project">GitHub repository</a>
        — vocabulary files, grammar sources, and working notes
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/L1ghth0us3/The-Huntspeak-Project/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md"
          >How to contribute</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Official in-game material is kept separate in the repo’s <code>canon/</code> folder. Where the
      game speaks, the game wins; everything else is community expansion.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
